{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.FreeEnergyReadingIsSigned","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.FreeEnergyReadingIsSigned","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FreeEnergySigned.pn_blockSum_eq_h_delta_half","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FreeEnergySigned.pn_blockSum_eq_h_delta_half","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FreeEnergyReadingIsSigned.lean#L140-L144","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FreeEnergySigned.blockSum_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FreeEnergySigned.blockSum_eq","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FreeEnergyReadingIsSigned.lean#L134-L138","doc":"The unweighted block sum, whose `pn` value is the probe's `h·δ/2`. Recorded\nbecause it is what makes the `pn` letter the near-null vector of the unweighted\nsum — it survives in `z + d` only because `w_+ ≠ w_-`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FreeEnergySigned.pn_pos_but_signed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FreeEnergySigned.pn_pos_but_signed","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FreeEnergyReadingIsSigned.lean#L127-L132","doc":"The `pn` instance, the letter the binding arc turns on. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FreeEnergySigned.nn_pos_but_signed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FreeEnergySigned.nn_pos_but_signed","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FreeEnergyReadingIsSigned.lean#L120-L125","doc":"The `nn` instance: `tr_2(sigma⁻¹) = z - h > 0`, `(1,1)` summand negative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FreeEnergySigned.pp_pos_but_signed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FreeEnergySigned.pp_pos_but_signed","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FreeEnergyReadingIsSigned.lean#L114-L118","doc":"The `pp` instance, with the positivity discharged from the arc's own lemma:\n`tr_2(sigma) = z > 0`, while its `(1,1)` summand is negative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FreeEnergySigned.stateSum_pos_but_signed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FreeEnergySigned.stateSum_pos_but_signed","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FreeEnergyReadingIsSigned.lean#L105-L112","doc":"**The state sum is positive overall and signed term by term.** That pairing\nis the whole finding: `L = -log(z + d)` is a real number, so nothing computed\nfrom it moves, and yet the object under the logarithm is not a partition\nfunction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FreeEnergySigned.admissible_letters_nonpos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FreeEnergySigned.admissible_letters_nonpos","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FreeEnergyReadingIsSigned.lean#L94-L103","doc":"The three interface letters the algebra supplies — `0`, `-h`, and `d_pn` —\nare all non-positive for `1 ≤ q` with `δ ≤ 2`, so the theorem above applies to\nevery one of them. (`-h/2` is the `δ = 0` case of `d_pn`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FreeEnergySigned.no_real_energy_for_minus_block","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FreeEnergySigned.no_real_energy_for_minus_block","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FreeEnergyReadingIsSigned.lean#L85-L92","doc":"**No real energy.** `exp` is positive; the `(1,1)` factor is not. So the\nblock carries no `E_-`, and the Legendre structure `F = U - TS` is absent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FreeEnergySigned.positivity_would_need_d_gt_inv_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FreeEnergySigned.positivity_would_need_d_gt_inv_q","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FreeEnergyReadingIsSigned.lean#L78-L83","doc":"Positivity of the `(1,1)` summand would need `d > q⁻¹`, and `q⁻¹ > 0`: the\nrequired offset is on the other side of ZERO from every non-positive letter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FreeEnergySigned.minusSummand_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FreeEnergySigned.minusSummand_neg","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FreeEnergyReadingIsSigned.lean#L74-L76","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FreeEnergySigned.minusFactor_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FreeEnergySigned.minusFactor_neg","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FreeEnergyReadingIsSigned.lean#L68-L72","doc":"**The `(1,1)` factor is negative** for every `q > 0` and every non-positive\noffset. This is the whole obstruction, and it needs no substrate value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FreeEnergySigned.wMinus_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FreeEnergySigned.wMinus_pos","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FreeEnergyReadingIsSigned.lean#L62-L66","doc":"The `(1,1)` Wenzl weight is strictly positive, so it cannot flip a sign. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FreeEnergySigned.qint3_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FreeEnergySigned.qint3_pos","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FreeEnergyReadingIsSigned.lean#L57-L60","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FreeEnergySigned.minusSummand","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FreeEnergySigned.minusSummand","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FreeEnergyReadingIsSigned.lean#L54-L55","doc":"The `(1,1)` block's summand of `tr_2(sigma + d)`: weight times factor. ","signatureChunk":0}]}